mal line to the curve $y=-2\sqrt[4]{x}-3$ at the point $(16,-7)$ intersects the $x$-axis.

The intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values."] [:db/add "b29dd078-2ebc-5d53-826e-4eebe7992cae" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.

$$
\begin{aligned}
f(x)&=- 2 x^{\frac{1}{4}} - 3, \\f'(x)&=- \frac{1}{2 x^{\frac{3}{4}}}=- \frac{1}{2 x^{\frac{3}{4}}}.
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.

$$
\begin{aligned}
m_t=f'(16)&=- \frac{1}{2 (16)^{\frac{3}{4}}}=- \frac{1}{16}, \\m_n=-\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\frac{1}{\left(- \frac{1}{16}\right)}=16.
\end{aligned}
$$

Use point-slope form through $(16,-7)$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-(-7)&=16(x-(16)), \\y&=16 x - 263.
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $x$-axis, $y=0$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
0&=16x+(-263), \\x&=\frac{263}{16}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The intersection is $\left(\frac{263}{16},0\right)$."] [:db/add "b29dd078-2ebc-5d53-826e-4eebe7992cae" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "b29dd078-2ebc-5d53-826e-4eebe7992cae" :question/answer-fields "3d28ea72-04ae-5db8-b62d-9aec5492882b"] [:db/add "b29dd078-2ebc-5d53-826e-4eebe7992cae" :question/answer-fields "9e991031-582e-5686-a53b-62bf31e1399b"] [:db/ensure "b29dd078-2ebc-5d53-826e-4eebe7992cae" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186092385 :knowledge-point/questions "b29dd078-2ebc-5d53-826e-4eebe7992cae"] [:db/add "edf92b3a-5431-50ab-beed-623ef07b5994" :answer/id #uuid "edf92b3a-5431-50ab-beed-623ef07b5994"] [:db/add "edf92b3a-5431-50ab-beed-623ef07b5994" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "edf92b3a-5431-50ab-beed-623ef07b5994" :answer/value "0"] [:db/ensure "edf92b3a-5431-50ab-beed-623ef07b5994" :answer/validate] [:db/add "71568e09-28aa-59ac-8ca3-5dbb95764716" :answer-field/id #uuid "71568e09-28aa-59ac-8ca3-5dbb95764716"] [:db/add "71568e09-28aa-59ac-8ca3-5dbb95764716" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "71568e09-28aa-59ac-8ca3-5dbb95764716" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "71568e09-28aa-59ac-8ca3-5dbb95764716" :answer-field/choices "edf92b3a-5431-50ab-beed-623ef07b5994"] [:db/add "71568e09-28aa-59ac-8ca3-5dbb95764716" :answer-field/correct "edf92b3a-5431-50ab-beed-623ef07b5994"] [:db/ensure "71568e09-28aa-59ac-8ca3-5dbb95764716" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "987575de-1233-554d-bad4-462cace7ab49" :answer/id #uuid "987575de-1233-554d-bad4-462cace7ab49"] [:db/add "987575de-1233-554d-bad4-462cace7ab49" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "987575de-1233-554d-bad4-462cace7ab49" :answer/value "- \frac{17}{3}"] [:db/ensure "987575de-1233-554d-bad4-462cace7ab49" :answer/validate] [:db/add "9fffbf35-c438-5860-919c-71e3071c2bff" :answer-field/id #uuid "9fffbf35-c438-5860-919c-71e3071c2bff"] [:db/add "9fffbf35-c438-5860-919c-71e3071c2bff" :answer-field/key "field-2"] [:db/add "9fffbf35-c438-5860-919c-71e3071c2bff" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "9fffbf35-c438-5860-919c-71e3071c2bff" :answer-field/choices "987575de-1233-554d-bad4-462cace7ab49"] [:db/add "9fffbf35-c438-5860-919c-71e3071c2bff" :answer-field/correct "987575de-1233-554d-bad4-462cace7ab49"] [:db/ensure "9fffbf35-c438-5860-919c-71e3071c2bff" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "faa54547-2c59-5b03-b679-878d5c36016f" :question/id #uuid "faa54547-2c59-5b03-b679-878d5c36016f"] [:db/add "faa54547-2c59-5b03-b679-878d5c36016f" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=-3\sqrt{x}-2$ at the point $(1,-5)$ intersects the $y$-axis.

The intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values."] [:db/add "faa54547-2c59-5b03-b679-878d5c36016f" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.

$$
\begin{aligned}
f(x)&=- 3 x^{\frac{1}{2}} - 2, \\f'(x)&=- \frac{3}{2 x^{\frac{1}{2}}}=- \frac{3}{2 \sqrt{x}}.
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.

$$
\begin{aligned}
m_t=f'(1)&=- \frac{3}{2 \sqrt{(1)}}=- \frac{3}{2}, \\m_n=-\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\frac{1}{\left(- \frac{3}{2}\right)}=\frac{2}{3}.
\end{aligned}
$$

Use point-slope form through $(1,-5)$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-(-5)&=\frac{2}{3}(x-(1)), \\y&=\frac{2 x}{3} - \frac{17}{3}.
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $y$-axis, $x=0$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
y&=\frac{2}{3}\cdot 0+\left(- \frac{17}{3}\right), \\y&=- \frac{17}{3}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The intersection is $\left(0,- \frac{17}{3}\right)$."] [:db/add "faa54547-2c59-5b03-b679-878d5c36016f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "faa54547-2c59-5b03-b679-878d5c36016f" :question/answer-fields "71568e09-28aa-59ac-8ca3-5dbb95764716"] [:db/add "faa54547-2c59-5b03-b679-878d5c36016f" :question/answer-fields "9fffbf35-c438-5860-919c-71e3071c2bff"] [:db/ensure "faa54547-2c59-5b03-b679-878d5c36016f" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186092385 :knowledge-point/questions "faa54547-2c59-5b03-b679-878d5c36016f"] [:db/add "9b36f04f-29a4-57f4-b792-3d8cddf7dbb7" :answer/id #uuid "9b36f04f-29a4-57f4-b792-3d8cddf7dbb7"] [:db/add "9b36f04f-29a4-57f4-b792-3d8cddf7dbb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "9b36f04f-29a4-57f4-b792-3d8cddf7dbb7" :answer/value "25"] [:db/ensure "9b36f04f-29a4-57f4-b792-3d8cddf7dbb7" :answer/validate] [:db/add "105f3b7c-32d3-5721-896a-80a7e4481dd8" :answer-field/id #uuid "105f3b7c-32d3-5721-896a-80a7e4481dd8"] [:db/add "105f3b7c-32d3-5721-896a-80a7e4481dd8" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "105f3b7c-32d3-5721-896a-80a7e4481dd8" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "105f3b7c-32d3-5721-896a-80a7e4481dd8" :answer-field/choices "9b36f04f-29a4-57f4-b792-3d8cddf7dbb7"] [:db/add "105f3b7c-32d3-5721-896a-80a7e4481dd8" :answer-field/correct "9b36f04f-29a4-57f4-b792-3d8cddf7dbb7"] [:db/ensure "105f3b7c-32d3-5721-896a-80a7e4481dd8" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "00e8d86d-1129-5622-a67f-6cdd2601671e" :answer/id #uuid "00e8d86d-1129-5622-a67f-6cdd2601671e"] [:db/add "00e8d86d-1129-5622-a67f-6cdd2601671e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "00e8d86d-1129-5622-a67f-6cdd2601671e" :answer/value "0"] [:db/ensure "00e8d86d-1129-5622-a67f-6cdd2601671e" :answer/validate] [:db/add "e756993e-1199-53fc-a2ee-d01738092d6f" :answer-field/id #uuid "e756993e-1199-53fc-a2ee-d01738092d6f"] [:db/add "e756993e-1199-53fc-a2ee-d01738092d6f" :answer-field/key "field-2"] [:db/add "e756993e-1199-53fc-a2ee-d01738092d6f" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "e756993e-1199-53fc-a2ee-d01738092d6f" :answer-field/choices "00e8d86d-1129-5622-a67f-6cdd2601671e"] [:db/add "e756993e-1199-53fc-a2ee-d01738092d6f" :answer-field/correct "00e8d86d-1129-5622-a67f-6cdd2601671e"] [:db/ensure "e756993e-1199-53fc-a2ee-d01738092d6f" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "2ed6c176-c8ce-5e49-a7ef-0346fa82cc02" :question/id #uuid "2ed6c176-c8ce-5e49-a7ef-0346fa82cc02"] [:db/add "2ed6c176-c8ce-5e49-a7ef-0346fa82cc02" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=\sqrt{x^{3}}-1$ at the point $(4,7)$ intersects the $x$-axis.

The intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values."] [:db/add "2ed6c176-c8ce-5e49-a7ef-0346fa82cc02" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.

$$
\begin{aligned}
f(x)&=x^{\frac{3}{2}} - 1, \\f'(x)&=\frac{3 x^{\frac{1}{2}}}{2}=\frac{3 \sqrt{x}}{2}.
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.

$$
\begin{aligned}
m_t=f'(4)&=\frac{3 \sqrt{(4)}}{2}=3, \\m_n=-\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\frac{1}{(3)}=- \frac{1}{3}.
\end{aligned}
$$

Use point-slope form through $(4,7)$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-(7)&=- \frac{1}{3}(x-(4)), \\y&=- \frac{x}{3} + \frac{25}{3}.
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $x$-axis, $y=0$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
0&=- \frac{1}{3}x+\left(\frac{25}{3}\right), \\x&=25.
\end{aligned}
$$

The intersection is $(25,0)$."] [:db/add "2ed6c176-c8ce-5e49-a7ef-0346fa82cc02" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "2ed6c176-c8ce-5e49-a7ef-0346fa82cc02" :question/answer-fields "105f3b7c-32d3-5721-896a-80a7e4481dd8"] [:db/add "2ed6c176-c8ce-5e49-a7ef-0346fa82cc02" :question/answer-fields "e756993e-1199-53fc-a2ee-d01738092d6f"] [:db/ensure "2ed6c176-c8ce-5e49-a7ef-0346fa82cc02" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186092385 :knowledge-point/questions "2ed6c176-c8ce-5e49-a7ef-0346fa82cc02"] [:db/add "4d6ce5d3-903a-5e82-90e6-9d71c4be85f4" :answer/id #uuid "4d6ce5d3-903a-5e82-90e6-9d71c4be85f4"] [:db/add "4d6ce5d3-903a-5e82-90e6-9d71c4be85f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "4d6ce5d3-903a-5e82-90e6-9d71c4be85f4" :answer/value "0"] [:db/ensure "4d6ce5d3-903a-5e82-90e6-9d71c4be85f4" :answer/validate] [:db/add "7a507089-6cf8-5df8-b8df-3ac97398dd75" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a507089-6cf8-5df8-b8df-3ac97398dd75"] [:db/add "7a507089-6cf8-5df8-b8df-3ac97398dd75" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "7a507089-6cf8-5df8-b8df-3ac97398dd75" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "7a507089-6cf8-5df8-b8df-3ac97398dd75" :answer-field/choices "4d6ce5d3-903a-5e82-90e6-9d71c4be85f4"] [:db/add "7a507089-6cf8-5df8-b8df-3ac97398dd75" :answer-field/correct "4d6ce5d3-903a-5e82-90e6-9d71c4be85f4"] [:db/ensure "7a507089-6cf8-5df8-b8df-3ac97398dd75" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "d88521b3-53b8-5a17-a4c2-f70e3754ec37" :answer/id #uuid "d88521b3-53b8-5a17-a4c2-f70e3754ec37"] [:db/add "d88521b3-53b8-5a17-a4c2-f70e3754ec37" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "d88521b3-53b8-5a17-a4c2-f70e3754ec37" :answer/value "17"] [:db/ensure "d88521b3-53b8-5a17-a4c2-f70e3754ec37" :answer/validate] [:db/add "963d8c9b-cc10-5c12-8b87-028a86b2e2b6" :answer-field/id #uuid "963d8c9b-cc10-5c12-8b87-028a86b2e2b6"] [:db/add "963d8c9b-cc10-5c12-8b87-028a86b2e2b6" :answer-field/key "field-2"] [:db/add "963d8c9b-cc10-5c12-8b87-028a86b2e2b6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "963d8c9b-cc10-5c12-8b87-028a86b2e2b6" :answer-field/choices "d88521b3-53b8-5a17-a4c2-f70e3754ec37"] [:db/add "963d8c9b-cc10-5c12-8b87-028a86b2e2b6" :answer-field/correct "d88521b3-53b8-5a17-a4c2-f70e3754ec37"] [:db/ensure "963d8c9b-cc10-5c12-8b87-028a86b2e2b6" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "29406d9f-bf1b-52ad-b004-ccc298593364" :question/id #uuid "29406d9f-bf1b-52ad-b004-ccc298593364"] [:db/add "29406d9f-bf1b-52ad-b004-ccc298593364" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=3\sqrt[3]{x^{2}}-3$ at the point $(8,9)$ intersects the $y$-axis.

The intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values."] [:db/add "29406d9f-bf1b-52ad-b004-ccc298593364" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.

$$
\begin{aligned}
f(x)&=3 x^{\frac{2}{3}} - 3, \\f'(x)&=\frac{2}{x^{\frac{1}{3}}}=\frac{2}{\sqrt[3]{x}}.
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.

$$
\begin{aligned}
m_t=f'(8)&=\frac{2}{\sqrt[3]{(8)}}=1, \\m_n=-\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\frac{1}{(1)}=-1.
\end{aligned}
$$

Use point-slope form through $(8,9)$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-(9)&=-1(x-(8)), \\y&=- x + 17.
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $y$-axis, $x=0$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
y&=-1\cdot 0+(17), \\y&=17.
\end{aligned}
$$

The intersection is $(0,17)$."] [:db/add "29406d9f-bf1b-52ad-b004-ccc298593364" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "29406d9f-bf1b-52ad-b004-ccc298593364" :question/answer-fields "7a507089-6cf8-5df8-b8df-3ac97398dd75"] [:db/add "29406d9f-bf1b-52ad-b004-ccc298593364" :question/answer-fields "963d8c9b-cc10-5c12-8b87-028a86b2e2b6"] [:db/ensure "29406d9f-bf1b-52ad-b004-ccc298593364" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186092385 :knowledge-point/questions "29406d9f-bf1b-52ad-b004-ccc298593364"] [:db/add "f5e6aff2-b373-5430-b1d1-8590f82466c7" :answer/id #uuid "f5e6aff2-b373-5430-b1d1-8590f82466c7"] [:db/add "f5e6aff2-b373-5430-b1d1-8590f82466c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "f5e6aff2-b373-5430-b1d1-8590f82466c7" :answer/value "\frac{11}{8}"] [:db/ensure "f5e6aff2-b373-5430-b1d1-8590f82466c7" :answer/validate] [:db/add "c0b9097b-e0d1-5242-9d99-bd382092dbc9" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0b9097b-e0d1-5242-9d99-bd382092dbc9"] [:db/add "c0b9097b-e0d1-5242-9d99-bd382092dbc9" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "c0b9097b-e0d1-5242-9d99-bd382092dbc9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "c0b9097b-e0d1-5242-9d99-bd382092dbc9" :answer-field/choices "f5e6aff2-b373-5430-b1d1-8590f82466c7"] [:db/add "c0b9097b-e0d1-5242-9d99-bd382092dbc9" :answer-field/correct "f5e6aff2-b373-5430-b1d1-8590f82466c7"] [:db/ensure "c0b9097b-e0d1-5242-9d99-bd382092dbc9" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "1bc39092-d8e9-5453-8c18-574cb938a383" :answer/id #uuid "1bc39092-d8e9-5453-8c18-574cb938a383"] [:db/add "1bc39092-d8e9-5453-8c18-574cb938a383" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "1bc39092-d8e9-5453-8c18-574cb938a383" :answer/value "0"] [:db/ensure "1bc39092-d8e9-5453-8c18-574cb938a383" :answer/validate] [:db/add "9f59a7a4-1543-5be4-a86a-343a53b151e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f59a7a4-1543-5be4-a86a-343a53b151e1"] [:db/add "9f59a7a4-1543-5be4-a86a-343a53b151e1" :answer-field/key "field-2"] [:db/add "9f59a7a4-1543-5be4-a86a-343a53b151e1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "9f59a7a4-1543-5be4-a86a-343a53b151e1" :answer-field/choices "1bc39092-d8e9-5453-8c18-574cb938a383"] [:db/add "9f59a7a4-1543-5be4-a86a-343a53b151e1" :answer-field/correct "1bc39092-d8e9-5453-8c18-574cb938a383"] [:db/ensure "9f59a7a4-1543-5be4-a86a-343a53b151e1" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5" :question/id #uuid "0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5"] [:db/add "0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5" :question/problem "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=\frac{1}{x}+2$ at the point $\left(2,\frac{5}{2}\right)$ intersects the $x$-axis.

The intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values."] [:db/add "0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.

$$
\begin{aligned}
f(x)&=2 + \frac{1}{x}, \\f'(x)&=- \frac{1}{x^{2}}=- \frac{1}{x^{2}}.
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.

$$
\begin{aligned}
m_t=f'(2)&=- \frac{1}{(2)^{2}}=- \frac{1}{4}, \\m_n=-\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\frac{1}{\left(- \frac{1}{4}\right)}=4.
\end{aligned}
$$

Use point-slope form through $\left(2,\frac{5}{2}\right)$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-\left(\frac{5}{2}\right)&=4(x-(2)), \\y&=4 x - \frac{11}{2}.
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $x$-axis, $y=0$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
0&=4x+\left(- \frac{11}{2}\right), \\x&=\frac{11}{8}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The intersection is $\left(\frac{11}{8},0\right)$."] [:db/add "0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5" :question/answer-fields "c0b9097b-e0d1-5242-9d99-bd382092dbc9"] [:db/add "0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5" :question/answer-fields "9f59a7a4-1543-5be4-a86a-343a53b151e1"] [:db/ensure "0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186092385 :knowledge-point/questions "0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5"] [:db/ensure 17592186092385 :knowledge-point/validate]]

