e $y=\frac{1}{x}+2$ at the point $\left(2,\frac{5}{2}\right)$ intersects the $x$-axis.

The intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values."] ["0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.

$$
\begin{aligned}
f(x)&=2 + \frac{1}{x}, \\f'(x)&=- \frac{1}{x^{2}}=- \frac{1}{x^{2}}.
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.

$$
\begin{aligned}
m_t=f'(2)&=- \frac{1}{(2)^{2}}=- \frac{1}{4}, \\m_n=-\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\frac{1}{\left(- \frac{1}{4}\right)}=4.
\end{aligned}
$$

Use point-slope form through $\left(2,\frac{5}{2}\right)$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-\left(\frac{5}{2}\right)&=4(x-(2)), \\y&=4 x - \frac{11}{2}.
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $x$-axis, $y=0$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
0&=4x+\left(- \frac{11}{2}\right), \\x&=\frac{11}{8}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The intersection is $\left(\frac{11}{8},0\right)$."] ["0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5" :question/answer-fields "c0b9097b-e0d1-5242-9d99-bd382092dbc9"] ["0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5" :question/answer-fields "9f59a7a4-1543-5be4-a86a-343a53b151e1"] [17592186092385 :knowledge-point/questions "0528d2f1-a7ca-57e0-815f-c74f80d05fe5"]] "retractions" []}
